      "content": "but it doesn't feel temporary. it feels permanent. like the \"me\" that mattered is just gone. everyone looks at me and sees a broken athlete, but there's nothing left inside to fix. i'm just inhabiting this physical thing that feels like a cage now. does it even make sense to keep trying to fix a person when the soul of who they were is already dead?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
